# ioBroker.snapmaker

Connects ioBroker to **Snapmaker 2.0** machines (primarily **A350**, including laser / CNC toolheads) via the local HTTP API:

1. **Connect** — `POST http://<host>:8080/api/v1/connect` → token; first time confirm on the touchscreen
2. **Status poll** — `GET http://<host>:8080/api/v1/status?token=<token>` — job file name, remaining/elapsed time, progress, status, toolhead, …

Scaffold already exists (create-adapter 3.1.5). Implement logic in `main.js` + `lib/` (e.g. `lib/snapmakerApi.js`).

## Naming & scope

- Adapter name: **`iobroker.snapmaker`**
- **Tested / primary target:** Snapmaker 2.0 A350 (10W laser available for testing)
- Other Snapmaker 2.0 (A150 / A250) may work best-effort; document as untested until confirmed
- **Out of scope (v1):** Artisan / J1 (SACP), U1 (Moonraker) — different protocols
- Keep a curated, VIS-friendly state tree — do not mirror every API field blindly

## Stack (match inventwo adapters)

- Plain **JavaScript** in `main.js` + `lib/` — no TypeScript build step; optional `npm run check`
- Admin UI via **jsonConfig** (`admin/jsonConfig.json`)
- HTTP: native `node:http` / `node:https` (no axios)
- Author / org: skvarel / inventwo (MIT)
- Repo: `https://github.com/inventwo/ioBroker.snapmaker`
- Node.js `>= 22`

